{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XjzotjvdBrevVfMM9eArAW","type":"tool_result","content":"1576\t    fn sumcheck_polys_batch_eval(\n1577\t        &mut self,\n1578\t        round: usize,\n1579\t        r_prev: EF,\n1580\t    ) -> Result<Vec<Vec<EF>>, LogupZerocheckError> {\n1581\t        let sp_deg = self.constraint_degree;\n1582\t\n1583\t        // Per-trace outputs (filled as we go)\n1584\t        let mut zc_out: Vec<Vec<EF>> = vec![vec![EF::ZERO; sp_deg]; self.n_per_trace.len()];\n1585\t        let mut logup_out: Vec<[Vec<EF>; 2]> =\n1586\t            vec![[vec![EF::ZERO; sp_deg], vec![EF::ZERO; sp_deg]]; self.n_per_trace.len()];\n1587\t\n1588\t        let mut late_eval: Vec<TraceCtx> = Vec::new(); // round == n_lift + 1\n1589\t        let mut early_eval: Vec<TraceCtx> = Vec::new(); // round <= n_lift\n1590\t\n1591\t        // ── Phase 1: Collect metadata, split into Case A / Case B (no CUDA calls) ──\n1592\t        // For Case B traces, we collect column pointers and sizing info to batch the\n1593\t        // interpolation into a single kernel launch.\n1594\t        struct CaseBMeta {\n1595\t            trace_idx: usize,\n1596\t            air_idx: usize,\n1597\t            n_lift: usize,\n1598\t            num_y: usize,\n1599\t            num_columns: usize, // total columns (selectors + preprocessed + mains)\n1600\t            interp_offset: usize, // element offset within the big interpolated buffer\n1601\t            matrix_offset: usize, // start index in the all_matrices array\n1602\t            num_matrices: usize,  // number of matrices for this trace\n1603\t            has_preprocessed: bool,\n1604\t            need_rot: bool,\n1605\t            has_constraints: bool,\n1606\t            has_interactions: bool,\n1607\t            norm_factor: F,\n1608\t        }\n1609\t        let mut case_b_traces: Vec<CaseBMeta> = Vec::new();\n1610\t        let mut all_matrices: Vec<InterpMatrixInfo> = Vec::new();\n1611\t        let mut total_interp_elems: usize = 0;\n1612\t\n1613\t        for (trace_idx, (&n, mats, sels, eq_3bs, public_vals, &air_idx)) in izip!(\n1614\t            self.n_per_trace.iter(),\n1615\t            self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter(),\n1616\t            self.sels_per_trace.iter(),\n1617\t            self.d_eq_3b_per_trace.iter(),\n1618\t            self.public_values_per_trace.iter(),\n1619\t            self.air_indices_per_trace.iter()\n1620\t        )\n1621\t        .enumerate()\n1622\t        {\n1623\t            let pk = &self.pk.per_air[air_idx];\n1624\t            let dag = &pk.vk.symbolic_constraints;\n1625\t            let has_constraints = dag.constraints.num_constraints() > 0;\n1626\t            let has_interactions = !dag.interactions.is_empty();\n1627\t            if !has_constraints && !has_interactions {\n1628\t                continue;\n1629\t            }\n1630\t\n1631\t            let n_lift = n.max(0) as usize;\n1632\t            let norm_factor_denom = 1 << (-n).max(0);\n1633\t            let norm_factor = F::from_usize(norm_factor_denom).inverse();\n1634\t            let has_preprocessed = pk.preprocessed_data.is_some();\n1635\t            let need_rot = pk.vk.params.need_rot;\n1636\t            let first_main_idx = usize::from(has_preprocessed);\n1637\t            let eq_xi_tree = &self.eq_xis[&n_lift];\n1638\t\n1639\t            if round > n_lift {\n1640\t                // Case A\n1641\t                if round == n_lift + 1 {\n1642\t                    // A.1: evaluate directly at (num_x=1, num_y=1)\n1643\t                    let prep_ptr = if has_preprocessed {\n1644\t                        MainMatrixPtrs {\n1645\t                            data: mats[0].buffer().as_ptr(),\n1646\t                            air_width: air_width_for_mat(need_rot, mats[0].width()),\n1647\t                        }\n1648\t                    } else {\n1649\t                        MainMatrixPtrs {\n1650\t                            data: std::ptr::null(),\n1651\t                            air_width: 0,\n1652\t                        }\n1653\t                    };\n1654\t                    let main_ptrs: Vec<MainMatrixPtrs<EF>> = mats[first_main_idx..]\n1655\t                        .iter()"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"56bc24eb-d9a0-4ad2-8690-031f38c3d9d4","uuid":"7b51c1d1-4c5a-4a53-9dca-4899add4b705","timestamp":"2026-04-15T18:55:40.498Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs","content":"    fn sumcheck_polys_batch_eval(\n        &mut self,\n        round: usize,\n        r_prev: EF,\n    ) -> Result<Vec<Vec<EF>>, LogupZerocheckError> {\n        let sp_deg = self.constraint_degree;\n\n        // Per-trace outputs (filled as we go)\n        let mut zc_out: Vec<Vec<EF>> = vec![vec![EF::ZERO; sp_deg]; self.n_per_trace.len()];\n        let mut logup_out: Vec<[Vec<EF>; 2]> =\n            vec![[vec![EF::ZERO; sp_deg], vec![EF::ZERO; sp_deg]]; self.n_per_trace.len()];\n\n        let mut late_eval: Vec<TraceCtx> = Vec::new(); // round == n_lift + 1\n        let mut early_eval: Vec<TraceCtx> = Vec::new(); // round <= n_lift\n\n        // ── Phase 1: Collect metadata, split into Case A / Case B (no CUDA calls) ──\n        // For Case B traces, we collect column pointers and sizing info to batch the\n        // interpolation into a single kernel launch.\n        struct CaseBMeta {\n            trace_idx: usize,\n            air_idx: usize,\n            n_lift: usize,\n            num_y: usize,\n            num_columns: usize, // total columns (selectors + preprocessed + mains)\n            interp_offset: usize, // element offset within the big interpolated buffer\n            matrix_offset: usize, // start index in the all_matrices array\n            num_matrices: usize,  // number of matrices for this trace\n            has_preprocessed: bool,\n            need_rot: bool,\n            has_constraints: bool,\n            has_interactions: bool,\n            norm_factor: F,\n        }\n        let mut case_b_traces: Vec<CaseBMeta> = Vec::new();\n        let mut all_matrices: Vec<InterpMatrixInfo> = Vec::new();\n        let mut total_interp_elems: usize = 0;\n\n        for (trace_idx, (&n, mats, sels, eq_3bs, public_vals, &air_idx)) in izip!(\n            self.n_per_trace.iter(),\n            self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter(),\n            self.sels_per_trace.iter(),\n            self.d_eq_3b_per_trace.iter(),\n            self.public_values_per_trace.iter(),\n            self.air_indices_per_trace.iter()\n        )\n        .enumerate()\n        {\n            let pk = &self.pk.per_air[air_idx];\n            let dag = &pk.vk.symbolic_constraints;\n            let has_constraints = dag.constraints.num_constraints() > 0;\n            let has_interactions = !dag.interactions.is_empty();\n            if !has_constraints && !has_interactions {\n                continue;\n            }\n\n            let n_lift = n.max(0) as usize;\n            let norm_factor_denom = 1 << (-n).max(0);\n            let norm_factor = F::from_usize(norm_factor_denom).inverse();\n            let has_preprocessed = pk.preprocessed_data.is_some();\n            let need_rot = pk.vk.params.need_rot;\n            let first_main_idx = usize::from(has_preprocessed);\n            let eq_xi_tree = &self.eq_xis[&n_lift];\n\n            if round > n_lift {\n                // Case A\n                if round == n_lift + 1 {\n                    // A.1: evaluate directly at (num_x=1, num_y=1)\n                    let prep_ptr = if has_preprocessed {\n                        MainMatrixPtrs {\n                            data: mats[0].buffer().as_ptr(),\n                            air_width: air_width_for_mat(need_rot, mats[0].width()),\n                        }\n                    } else {\n                        MainMatrixPtrs {\n                            data: std::ptr::null(),\n                            air_width: 0,\n                        }\n                    };\n                    let main_ptrs: Vec<MainMatrixPtrs<EF>> = mats[first_main_idx..]\n                        .iter()","numLines":80,"startLine":1576,"totalLines":2310}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SpnKUVsB7ndsasVn953wDW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, I see the pattern now. The `sumcheck_polys_batch_eval` function is called each round and iterates over ALL traces to classify them (Case A vs Case B), collect metadata, build descriptor arrays, etc. This CPU iteration over 312+ traces × 14 rounds = 4368 iterations is the main overhead.\n\nThe key insight for optimization: The Case A/B partition for each trace is PREDICTABLE from the initial `n_lift` values and the round number. We can pre-compute which traces are Case A and which are Case B for every round.\n\nBut the actual descriptor building (collecting pointer arrays, building InterpMatrixInfo, etc.) depends on the current matrix pointers (which change after fold). This is harder to pre-compute.\n \nFor the fold phase though, the buffer layout is completely deterministic and doesn't depend on runtime state. So I can pre-compute the entire fold descriptor structure upfront, eliminating the per-round CPU overhead of collecting trace metadata and building descriptor arrays — that's 14 rounds × 2 fold operations × 4 H2D transfers plus all the trace iteration loops that could be collapsed into a single precomputation pass.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the eval phase since it has multiple kernel types each requiring their own descriptors. But no, the fold descriptor pre-upload is the most straightforward win here — it's well-defined and directly addresses the bottleneck.\n\nWait, I need to be more precise about where the actual cost is. The H2D bandwidth itself is minimal, maybe 6 microseconds per round. The real culprit is the CPU-side work: collecting vectors of trace data, allocating device buffers, and calling to_device() which chains together cudaMallocAsync, cudaMemcpyAsync, and then cudaFreeAsync after the kernel completes. That's 12 async operations per round that could be eliminated by