{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_014ZRKw5uhMy76XveZjd2Wo6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SHKkNxFTfFQn6crGSVj6ik","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-15-2100-precompute-mle-fold-layout\n\nMLE Rounds is the most anti-scaling STARK component: it takes 166ms at APC 300 vs 118ms at APC 0 (0.71x ratio), even though APC 300 has 2.35x fewer cells. The cause is per-round overhead in `fold_mle_evals`, which rebuilds and uploads 4 descriptor arrays (input_ptrs, output_ptrs, log_heights, widths) per fold call, twice per round (mat_evals + selectors), across 14 rounds — totaling 112 DeviceBuffer allocations + H2D uploads + frees per segment. Since fold buffer layouts are fully determined by initial trace heights/widths and the pingpong scheme, all descriptors can be pre-computed once and bulk-uploaded before the MLE loop, and the two per-round fold calls can be fused into a single kernel launch, eliminating per-round descriptor overhead and halving fold kernel launches.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11180,"cache_read_input_tokens":155131,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11180},"output_tokens":38,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"56bc24eb-d9a0-4ad2-8690-031f38c3d9d4","uuid":"40158e59-5b4a-4e02-a991-b99772a4bf02"}
