{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KqSvkqcS5Kw2dcDf7oPx5K","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-15-2100-precompute-mle-fold-layout\n2\t\n3\tMLE Rounds is the most anti-scaling STARK component: it takes 166ms at APC 300 vs 118ms at APC 0 (0.71x ratio), even though APC 300 has 2.35x fewer cells. The cause is per-round overhead in `fold_mle_evals`, which rebuilds and uploads 4 descriptor arrays (input_ptrs, output_ptrs, log_heights, widths) per fold call, twice per round (mat_evals + selectors), across 14 rounds — totaling 112 DeviceBuffer allocations + H2D uploads + frees per segment. Since fold buffer layouts are fully determined by initial trace heights/widths and the pingpong scheme, all descriptors can be pre-computed once and bulk-uploaded before the MLE loop, and the two per-round fold calls can be fused into a single kernel launch, eliminating per-round descriptor overhead and halving fold kernel launches.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019Y19crgSLWg4D2QajbpxKP","session_id":"56bc24eb-d9a0-4ad2-8690-031f38c3d9d4","uuid":"9c863ac3-741f-4f09-b776-d7490a9537b3","timestamp":"2026-04-15T19:02:14.714Z"}
